    <headline>Heavy Rain Risk Area</headline>
    <description>The high-pressure system from China covers upper Thailand and the South China Sea leading to the easterly wind prevails over the Gulf while the monsoon trough lies across the lower South with isolated heavy rains in the South.

 In the Andaman Sea and the Gulf, the waves will be higher than 2 meters high in thundershower areas.</description>
    <instruction> People in the South should beware of heavy rains and accumulations that may cause flash flood and overflows, especially along the waterways near foothills and lowlands. 

All ships should keep off thundershowers.</instruction>
